ons_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro","user_view_type":"public"}],"author_association":"NONE","body":"### Description\n\nI am trying to implement an operation that involves sharding an array along the leading axis followed by swapping the leading axis with axis 2, and finally, resharding along the new leading axis. This operations works fine on most configurations. However, It doesn't appear to work on a particular hardware configuration - 8 x Nvidia H100 80GB SMX5. \n\nHere's a minimal example to reproduce the issue:\n\n\n`import os\n\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\n\ndevices = jax.devices()\nnum_devices = len(devices)\n\nfrom jax.sharding import Mesh, PartitionSpec, NamedSharding\n\nmesh = Mesh(devices, (\"devices\",))\nspec = PartitionSpec(\"devices\",)\nsharding = NamedSharding(mesh, spec)\n\nx = jax.random.normal(jax.random.key(0), (num_devices, 2, num_devices, 3))\nx = jax.lax.with_sharding_constraint(x, sharding)\nx = jnp.swapaxes(x, 0, 2)\nx = jnp.reshape(x, (-1, 3)) # Program crashes here\nx = jax.lax.with_sharding_constraint(x, sharding)\nx = jnp.reshape(x, (num_devices, 2*num_devices, 3))\n`\n\n### System info (python version, jaxlib version, accelerator, etc.)\n\nAccelerator: 8 x Nvidia H100 80GB SMX5. \nOS: Ubuntu Linux\nHardware: x86_64\n\nJAX version: 0.5.2\nFlax version 0.10.6\n\nNVIDIA-SMI 570.148.08            \nDriver Version: 570.148.08     \nCUDA Version: 12.8 \n","closed_at":"2025-07-24T04:16:19Z","closed_by":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128307105?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/novastar53/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.gith